WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.080
Westworld Season 2 Episode 1 – what happens,
and what does it mean?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.259
We see Bernard during the massacre that Dolores
started last season.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:14.309
The host Rebus is shooting at a guest, just
like the guests had been shooting at him.

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:20.020
With Dolores’ robot rebellion, hosts are
getting bloody revenge on humanity.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.920
Bernard is hiding with Charlotte, and some
guests from the Delos corporate board.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.470
A friendly stable boy host comes in, and the
guests kill him because they don’t trust

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:34.280
any robot . Bernard is a robot, so he’ll
have to keep that secret to stay safe around

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.280
humans.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.480
On the way to an outpost, the guests are killed
by Angela and the masked men, who are working

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.640
for Dolores in her role as the villain Wyatt.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.220
Charlotte and Bernard escape to a secret Delos
lab, where drone hosts are working on… something.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:53.620
There were hints last season that Delos has
a “secret project” in Westworld . Apparently,

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:58.670
this involves recording Westworld “guests'
experiences and their DNA” . That kind of

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.680
data would be valuable.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.400
Rich and powerful people come to Westworld
, and if Delos has video footage of them killing

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.740
and fucking in the park, they could blackmail
powerful people for political influence – like

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:17.640
some kinda pee tape situation . And with guest
DNA, Delos could clone people.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.130
The 1976 Westworld sequel Futureworld has
Delos replacing world leaders with robot clones.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:28.560
So maybe Delos plans to use this data and
DNA to blackmail and replace people to…

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.400
y’know, take over the world.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.360
Charlotte asks Delos to come rescue them from
the robots, but Delos refuses until Charlotte

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.549
delivers Peter Abernathy . Last season, Charlotte
loaded Peter’s brain with important data

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:44.400
– maybe it’s this experience and DNA data.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.630
Charlotte tried to smuggle Pete to Delos,
but he didn’t make it.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:52.220
So now, Charlotte needs to find Abernathy
and get him to Delos, so that Charlotte can

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:55.470
escape and Delos can advance their plan.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:02:00.619
But maybe Dolores will get involved here – because
Abernathy is her host father.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:06.080
We see inside a host’s head, and their brain
is like an egg or pearl thing.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.610
Inside that is some red juice, which might
relate to this red nano stuff we saw in the

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.610
trailer.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:16.000
Bernard’s having problems with his brain
– probably because he shot himself last

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.000
season.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.270
His cortical shield is damaged , so he’s
leaking brain fluid out his ear.

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:26.680
He’s shaking, and confused, and nearly dies,
until he takes brain fluid from another host

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.090
and injects it to himself, like some kind
of robot vampire.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:37.110
This is probably just a temporary fix – maybe
he needs the help of Elsie for repairs.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:43.020
Earlier in the episode, we see Bernard wake
up on a beach with Delos forces Karl Strand,

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.750
Antoine and Maling.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:50.080
This stuff actually happens two weeks after
the bits with Charlotte and Dolores’ massacre.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.930
Bernard is “unstuck in time” , and has
flashbacks of stuff that may have happened

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.849
over the last couple weeks – future episodes
might fill in these blanks.

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:02.190
Strand’s men are mopping up after Dolores’
uprising.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.520
They execute hosts , which disturbs Bernard.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.930
He’s sympathetic to his fellow robots.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.530
And yet here he is helping the humans.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:16.430
So Bernard feels deeply “conflicted” . Strand
talks to some Chinese military guys, and says

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:21.030
“[their] country” has given Delos control
over “this … island” . This seems to

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:25.709
confirm that Westworld is an island on Earth,
probably near China.

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:30.340
The Finnish subtitles of the Season 1 finale
give coordinates to a place in the South China

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:35.950
Sea called Mischief Reef , where in the real
world China is building artificial islands

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.200
. So this seems to be the true location of
Westworld.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:45.010
Stubbs turns up, which is mysterious, cause
last we saw him, he was captured by hosts

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.440
from Ghost Nation.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.620
How did he escape?

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.489
What did Ghost Nation want?

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:52.590
Why is no one talking about Stubbs’ disappearance?

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.620
It seems suspicious.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.310
Bernard goes with Strand to look for missing
hosts.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:04:03.680
They find a Bengal tiger, wandered across
from Park 6 . Park 1 is Westworld, and Shogun

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.490
World seems to be Park 2 – so what’s Park
6?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.739
Well Bengal tigers are from India.

00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:14.461
And a Reddit user found a hidden image on
a Westworld site that says Rajworld , maybe

00:04:14.461 --> 00:04:17.349
meaning the Rajasthan region of India.

00:04:17.349 --> 00:04:21.959
So maybe Park 6 is an Indian themed park – with
tigers.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:26.420
Strand tracks the hosts to a place called
Western Valley . And they find the Valley

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:29.770
has inexplicably changed to a sea.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.999
Ford had used terraforming technology to shape
the land in Westworld, but Stubbs says they

00:04:34.999 --> 00:04:39.689
would’ve noticed if Ford had made this sea
while he was alive . And the water is full

00:04:39.689 --> 00:04:43.199
of hosts, including what looks like Teddy.

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:48.919
Bernard says that he killed all these hosts
. But how would Bernard do that, and why?

00:04:48.919 --> 00:04:51.430
This might connect to Dolores.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:55.849
At the start of the episode, we see Dolores
with Arnold – the human from thirty years

00:04:55.849 --> 00:04:58.759
ago who robot Bernard is based on.

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:02.099
Or maybe this is just Bernard in a vision
or something.

00:05:02.099 --> 00:05:07.080
Either way BernArnold tells her he had dream
he was “on an ocean”, and Dolores had

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.680
“left [him] behind”, and “the waters
were rising around [him]” – which sounds

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.719
like this flooded valley.

00:05:13.719 --> 00:05:18.539
BernArnold says he’s “frightened of what
[Dolores] might become” . And in this episode,

00:05:18.539 --> 00:05:21.159
Dolores becomes an anime supervillain.

00:05:21.159 --> 00:05:27.419
She guns down fleeing people, slowly executes
random humans, and gives a speech about the

00:05:27.419 --> 00:05:32.800
“reckoning” . She dehumanises her human
victims the same way humans dehumanised hosts,

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:36.840
calling them “things” , with “drive”s
and “cornerstone”s.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:41.520
Dolores says she feels conflicted between
different roles – she has the optimism and

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.669
compassion of Dolores, but also the cynicism
and brutality of Wyatt.

00:05:46.669 --> 00:05:52.169
Wyatt was a bad guy character who Arnold merged
with Dolores thirty years ago.

00:05:52.169 --> 00:05:58.059
Dolores wants to reject the Wyatt and Dolores
roles, and evolve into a new person . But

00:05:58.059 --> 00:06:01.159
so far, Dolores is mostly just acting like
Wyatt.

00:06:01.159 --> 00:06:05.909
She’s murdering random people, working with
Angela and the masked men, and talks about

00:06:05.909 --> 00:06:09.460
taking over the world . Wyatt was the same.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:15.509
He wanted to “claim this earth or raze it
to the ground” . So is Dolores truly free,

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:19.169
or is she still following her programming
as Wyatt?

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:24.839
Dolores says she remembers everything, and
that she has a special destiny with Teddy

00:06:24.839 --> 00:06:28.930
. How does that connect to Teddy’s drowning
in the valley?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:34.080
We see Dolores kill a host, and say “not
all of us deserve to make it to the valley

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:39.699
beyond” . The stable boy mentions riding
for “the valley beyond” . And Rebus mentions

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:44.960
“the journey” . Is Dolores leading the
hosts on a “journey” to the flooded “valley”?

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.780
Is this part of the Wyatt storyline?

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:53.520
Wyatt seems like a Colonel Kurtz culty kinda
cunt – he’s got “strange ideas”, “Forces

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.919
his men to wear the … flesh of their enemies”,
and his followers “do anything for him”

00:06:58.919 --> 00:07:04.490
. Maybe Dolores is planning a mass death Jonestown
thing in the flooded valley.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:08.969
Dolores says it ends with Teddy, and Teddy’s
surname is Flood.

00:07:08.969 --> 00:07:14.189
The flood could connect to the Biblical flood,
where God wipes out humanity for being unworthy

00:07:14.189 --> 00:07:17.659
– like how Dolores is killing unworthy humans.

00:07:17.659 --> 00:07:20.759
But why would Dolores kill all these hosts?

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:25.990
Showrunner Jonathon Nolan says host “brains
don’t require oxygen” – so can hosts

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.029
even drown?

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:29.169
Are these hosts really dead?

00:07:29.169 --> 00:07:31.529
The flooding of the valley is very mysterious.

00:07:31.529 --> 00:07:36.419
But it seems connected to Dolores and Wyatt
and Teddy and Bernard.

00:07:36.419 --> 00:07:40.159
William, the Man in Black, emerges from corpses.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:43.719
He looks at that wolf that keeps turning up
at massacres.

00:07:43.719 --> 00:07:48.389
This wolf is one of the most baffling mysteries
in Westworld, no one knows what it means.

00:07:48.389 --> 00:07:51.599
Is it a symbol of death, consciousness, humanity?

00:07:51.599 --> 00:07:54.509
Or just a cute doggo that likes dead people?

00:07:54.509 --> 00:07:56.560
Maybe we’ll find out later on.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.840
William heads to a safehouse, and ends up
in a brutal fight with some hosts.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:06.539
He kills them with gun and knife, then treats
his wound, grunting and bleeding, then – he

00:08:06.539 --> 00:08:07.539
smiles.

00:08:07.539 --> 00:08:11.120
Cause this violence and pain is what William
wants.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:16.459
He calls it “fun” . He’s almost like
a darker version of Saitama in One Punch Man

00:08:16.459 --> 00:08:22.459
– someone who has power and freedom but
no purpose, so uses violence to distract himself

00:08:22.459 --> 00:08:28.169
from existential boredom . Westworld is set
in the future – maybe as technology and

00:08:28.169 --> 00:08:33.209
prosperity make modern life easier , people
lose the conflict and struggle that gives

00:08:33.209 --> 00:08:34.669
life meaning.

00:08:34.669 --> 00:08:41.089
So William seeks ever more challenge and violence
. He meets Robert, the robot version of a

00:08:41.089 --> 00:08:42.629
young Robert Ford.

00:08:42.629 --> 00:08:46.870
And Robert speaks to William with Ford’s
voice, congratulating him for finishing the

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:52.190
Maze goose chase last season, and giving him
a new quest – to “find the door”.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.100
To “make it back out”.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.319
Does this mean for William to escape the Westworld
park?

00:08:57.319 --> 00:08:59.579
Or is it more metaphorical?

00:08:59.579 --> 00:09:05.280
Robert says “The game begins where you end
… and ends where you began” , so maybe

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:09.390
William will go back to his past with Dolores,
and Logan.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:14.829
Robert says “Everything is code here”
– code because people speak in cryptic metaphor,

00:09:14.829 --> 00:09:19.600
and because hosts are programmed with computer
code – which reflects the connection between

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.550
secrets and control in this show.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:26.980
And then William shoots the kid on the face,
because– Westworld, and also to show that

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:30.129
Robert Ford is finally truly dead.

00:09:30.129 --> 00:09:33.940
There’s no robot decoy, no horcrux, no senzu
bean.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:40.149
Ford’s gone for good – at least until
HBO gets Hopkins back for some flashbacks.

00:09:40.149 --> 00:09:45.300
In the Mesa Hub, Sizemore is attacked by a
host that he designed back in Season 1.

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:48.240
He’s terrorised by lines that he wrote.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:52.850
He’s saved by Maeve who has the power to
control other hosts.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:58.370
They find the park control room’s been wiped
out – though it’s not clear who did this.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.880
Bernard’s flashback suggests that we’ll
learn more.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:06.569
Maeve recruits Sizemore to help her find her
daughter . Sizemore says Maeve’s daughter

00:10:06.569 --> 00:10:10.459
isn’t real – she’s just a robot that
was programmed to be her daughter . Maeve

00:10:10.459 --> 00:10:15.190
argues that she is artificial, but she still
has thoughts and feelings and the power to

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:20.689
splatter Sizemore on the walls . This argument
over realness connects back to Dolores and

00:10:20.689 --> 00:10:25.660
BernArnold’s conversation, and the idea
that something is “real” when it’s “irreplaceable”

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:31.360
– like, the robots of Westworld can be rebuilt
and replaced, whereas a human is unique.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.850
The irony is that Bernard is a robot replacement
of Arnold.

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:39.949
There are whole closets full of spare Bernards
– so is Bernard not real?

00:10:39.949 --> 00:10:43.270
And since Arnold was replaced – was Arnold
not real?

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:47.779
The technology of Westworld breaks down the
line between real and not-real.

00:10:47.779 --> 00:10:51.689
As far as Maeve cares, she loves her daughter,
so she goes to find her.

00:10:51.689 --> 00:10:56.220
Let’s hope she doesn’t find a closet full
of daughters, cause that sorta philosophy

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:59.540
quandary could really ruin a reunion.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:03.980
On the rooftop, Maeve reunites with Hector,
who was her sidekick in the rebellion last

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:04.980
season.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:09.279
Hector doesn’t care that Maeve left him
for dead, he’s just happy to follow her.

00:11:09.279 --> 00:11:13.800
So there’s a sort of romance between Maeve
and Hector, but is Hector acting of his own

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:14.970
free will?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:20.000
Maeve has the power to control other hosts
– and she fiddled with Hector’s programming.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.490
So is Hector’s loyalty real?

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:26.589
How is any relationship real if you can control
the people around you?

00:11:26.589 --> 00:11:30.100
How might this affect Maeve’s relationship
with her daughter?

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:34.689
Maeve makes Sizemore strip naked – just
like the Westworld techs strip hosts naked

00:11:34.689 --> 00:11:40.709
. Like Rebus and Dolores, Maeve is making
humans suffer the same way humans made hosts

00:11:40.709 --> 00:11:41.709
suffer.

00:11:41.709 --> 00:11:43.879
And there is a sort of justice to that.

00:11:43.879 --> 00:11:48.410
But last season, there was hope that the hosts
would choose to be better and nobler than

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:53.410
humanity . Doesn’t killing and hurting make
them just as bad as us?

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.259
This season explores “the birth of a new
people.

00:11:56.259 --> 00:11:58.560
And the choices they … make”.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:04.329
What choices will Dolores, Maeve and Bernard
make to shape the destiny of this new robot

00:12:04.329 --> 00:12:05.680
people?

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:11.060
In Season 1, Ford compares robot-human war
to the conflict between humans and Neanderthals

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:16.430
forty thousand years ago . This is a story
told in Sapiens, by Yuval Harari.

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:21.490
The book is a quick history of our species
– from the evolution of consciousness, to

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.649
language, religion, money, agriculture.

00:12:23.649 --> 00:12:26.899
science, all explained clearly and accessibly.

